  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fifth Global Summit of Strong Cities Network In Cape Town, South Africa from 3-5 December 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">?The Summit will convene mayors and other local leaders, local government practitioners, civil society actors and national and international partners to showcase how cities are preventing and responding to hate, extremism and polarisation. it will provide a platform for city officials to share innovative solutions for safeguarding human rights and strengthening social cohesion amid consecutive crises such as unprecedented levels of migration and urbanisation caused by climate change, the consequent competition over resources and increased anti-migrant sentiment and violence as well as mis/disinformation and consequences for social cohesion during elections. The Summit will launch Strong Cities&apos; Women&apos;s Local Leadership Caucus, showcasing the contribution of women local officials and allow women to share the gender-based threats they are often subject to.</narrative>
  </description>
